  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Capacities for Disaster-ready Communities through Anticipatory Action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact -based disaster parametric forecasting. In reference to the Parametric Index on typhoon developed under BREADY3, data will be collected from the communities of 5 municipalities  - Lawaan, Quinapondan, Salcedo, Balangiga, Dolores Eastern Samar Philippines, including their other vulnerabilities such as access to finance and resources, income levels and vulnerable groups. This will be the reference in developing Municipal level &quot;triggers&quot; protocol for typhoon which serves as guidelines that tell communities when to activate Anticipatory Action (AA). &#x2022; Pre -emptive disaster financing. Local Government Unit will use parametric -based trigger index as a basis for anticipatory action through unconditional (pre -emptive) cash transfer/vouchers (depending on market access and functionality). This innovation is built on what Oxfam (through Strengthening Harmonised Action for Disaster Riske Reduction (DRR), Preparedness and Early action and Recovery (SHARPER) and BREADY project) is already doing, which combines digital financial services to be available online and be accessible in different forms, as inspired by the platform developed for iAFFORD4 where the cardholders have access to financial accounts and use the cards to receive funds and facilitate savings, remittance, payments, and insurance. When there is a trigger for release, money will be automatically transferred to the 600 registered mobile (target project participants from the 6 municipalities) numbers and the linked cards. A total of Php 2,000.00 will be released to the project participants based on the government daily minimum wage (equivalent to 3 days). &#x2022; Assessing viability of forecast -based insurance as a form of early warning system and risk transfer mechanism. Oxfam commissioned CelsiusPro AG5 to draft a Proof of Concept (PoC) to transform pre -emptive parametric -triggered cash transfers into a pre -emptive insurance pay out. Based on initial results, PoC is scalable even up to a national level, while still</narrative>
  </description>
